1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:06,149
You're swimming at the beach, when the ocean around you turns into a giant checkerboard.

2
00:00:06,199 --> 00:00:08,389
Perfect squares, stretching to the horizon.

3
00:00:08,439 --> 00:00:09,509
It looks amazing.

4
00:00:09,559 --> 00:00:14,362
It is also one of the most dangerous things the sea can do.

5
00:00:14,412 --> 00:00:18,468
Today, seven warning signs from nature that you should never ignore.

6
00:00:18,518 --> 00:00:20,708
And stick around for number two.

7
00:00:20,758 --> 00:00:23,694
It might be hiding in your own backyard.

8
00:00:25,044 --> 00:00:25,769
Number seven.

9
00:00:25,819 --> 00:00:26,544
Square waves.

10
00:00:26,594 --> 00:00:29,643
This checkerboard pattern is called a cross sea.

11
00:00:29,693 --> 00:00:37,004
It happens when two wave systems collide at nearly a right angle, usually left over from two different storms.

12
00:00:37,054 --> 00:00:43,590
It looks calm from the beach, but underneath, powerful currents are pulling in two directions at once.

13
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:48,627
Boats struggle to steer through it, and even strong swimmers tire out fast.

14
00:00:48,677 --> 00:00:57,150
If the water starts to look like a chessboard, swim parallel to the shore until the pattern ends, then head straight in.

15
00:00:58,500 --> 00:00:59,214
Number six.

16
00:00:59,264 --> 00:01:00,743
The ocean suddenly disappears.

17
00:01:00,793 --> 00:01:09,531
If the water pulls back hundreds of feet past low tide, leaving fish flopping on the sand, do not walk out to explore.

18
00:01:09,581 --> 00:01:13,734
A sudden ocean retreat is nature's final warning before a tsunami.

19
00:01:13,784 --> 00:01:15,645
The water is not gone.

20
00:01:15,695 --> 00:01:19,466
It is being pulled back, to return as a wall.

21
00:01:19,516 --> 00:01:24,433
From the moment the sea vanishes, you may have less than five minutes.

22
00:01:24,483 --> 00:01:28,254
Drop everything, move to high ground, and do not stop.

23
00:01:29,604 --> 00:01:30,313
Number five.

24
00:01:30,363 --> 00:01:31,452
A green sky.

25
00:01:31,502 --> 00:01:34,109
Storm clouds are supposed to be gray.

26
00:01:34,159 --> 00:01:45,495
If the sky turns the color of pea soup, those clouds are so tall, and so packed with water and ice, that they filter sunlight the way an ocean does.

27
00:01:45,545 --> 00:01:48,911
Clouds like that love producing giant hail, and tornadoes.

28
00:01:48,961 --> 00:01:56,882
Get inside, stay away from the windows, and if you live in tornado country, make the basement your new favorite room.

29
00:01:58,232 --> 00:01:58,954
Number four.

30
00:01:59,004 --> 00:02:00,883
The calm patch of water.

31
00:02:00,933 --> 00:02:07,829
You scan the sea, and one channel looks perfectly smooth, while waves break on either side of it.

32
00:02:07,879 --> 00:02:10,530
That quiet lane is a rip current.

33
00:02:10,580 --> 00:02:16,317
A conveyor belt of water rushing away from the beach, faster than an Olympic swimmer.

34
00:02:16,367 --> 00:02:19,404
If it grabs you, do not fight it.

35
00:02:19,454 --> 00:02:25,192
Float, keep breathing, and swim sideways, parallel to the beach, until you escape the belt.

36
00:02:25,242 --> 00:02:28,279
Then let the waves carry you back home.

37
00:02:28,329 --> 00:02:31,366
Panic is the real danger, not the water.

38
00:02:32,716 --> 00:02:33,387
Number three.

39
00:02:33,437 --> 00:02:35,552
Trees shaped like the letter J.

40
00:02:35,602 --> 00:02:39,880
Trees cannot move, so they write their life story in their trunks.

41
00:02:39,930 --> 00:02:51,424
When every tree on a hillside curves at the base and straightens at the top, the ground beneath them is slowly sliding downhill, and the trees keep correcting themselves as it creeps.

42
00:02:51,474 --> 00:02:53,227
One bent tree means nothing.

43
00:02:53,277 --> 00:02:57,556
A whole slope of them means landslide country, especially after heavy rain.

44
00:02:57,606 --> 00:03:02,606
Not the place for a picnic, and definitely not the place for a house.

45
00:03:03,956 --> 00:03:04,589
Number two.

46
00:03:04,639 --> 00:03:07,663
A perfect circle of dead grass in your yard.

47
00:03:07,713 --> 00:03:10,396
Told you this one was close to home.

48
00:03:10,446 --> 00:03:19,959
If the grass dies in a ring, and the center feels soft and sunken when you step on it, you might be standing on a sinkhole in progress.

49
00:03:20,009 --> 00:03:25,424
Underground water slowly dissolves the rock below, and the surface is the last thing to know.

50
00:03:25,474 --> 00:03:33,963
If doors in your house suddenly refuse to close, and new cracks appear above your windows, do not test the spot by jumping on it.

51
00:03:34,013 --> 00:03:38,062
Rope it off, keep kids and pets away, and call an engineer.

52
00:03:39,412 --> 00:03:40,560
And number one.

53
00:03:40,610 --> 00:03:42,157
The forest goes silent.

54
00:03:42,207 --> 00:03:47,746
Birds chirping, insects buzzing, and then, in the space of a few seconds, nothing.

55
00:03:47,796 --> 00:03:50,141
Animals go quiet for one reason.

56
00:03:50,191 --> 00:03:52,536
Something they fear has just arrived.

57
00:03:52,586 --> 00:03:55,331
It could be a predator moving through.

58
00:03:55,381 --> 00:03:57,726
It could be a coming storm.

59
00:03:57,776 --> 00:04:02,916
Whatever it is, thousands of ears better than yours just voted to hide.

60
00:04:02,966 --> 00:04:06,908
Stop, look around, and move calmly back toward open ground.

61
00:04:06,958 --> 00:04:12,098
You do not need to know what the danger is, to respect it.

62
00:04:13,448 --> 00:04:17,436
So here is the golden rule that covers all seven.

63
00:04:17,486 --> 00:04:24,705
When nature suddenly changes its behavior, the water, the sky, the sound, that is not a photo opportunity.

64
00:04:24,755 --> 00:04:26,320
That is a message.

65
00:04:26,370 --> 00:04:27,128
Quick recap.

66
00:04:27,178 --> 00:04:29,147
Square waves mean crossing currents.

67
00:04:29,197 --> 00:04:31,166
A vanishing ocean means tsunami.

68
00:04:31,216 --> 00:04:33,993
A green sky means hail and tornadoes.

69
00:04:34,043 --> 00:04:36,416
A calm channel means rip current.

70
00:04:36,466 --> 00:04:38,435
Bent trees mean sliding ground.

71
00:04:38,485 --> 00:04:41,262
A ring of dead grass means sinkhole.

72
00:04:41,312 --> 00:04:43,685
And silence means something is coming.

73
00:04:43,735 --> 00:04:46,915
Read the signs, and you will be fine.

74
00:04:46,965 --> 00:04:54,588
If this video taught you something new, share it with a friend who needs it, and subscribe for more.

75
00:04:54,638 --> 00:04:59,030
Stay safe, stay curious, and see you in the next one.
